        verification storyStpaDiagramInTheBinaryDoD : Test { :>> id = "51dc7abe-74ff-4c3b-b83a-4cd08154b81f"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "The DoD of dcStpaDiagramInTheBinary: keel show control-structure --svg draws the diagram in the binary. keel-cli/src/view/stpa_diagram.rs is a port of the Python tool's layout and serialisation with Python's int/float arithmetic reproduced (Num), and port_is_byte_equal_to_the_python_tool_on_the_same_json holds the render against the golden SVG the Python tool wrote for the fixture JSON (keel-cli/tests/fixtures/stpa/). On the live tree the render function's output equals HEAD's Python tool's output byte for byte on the same JSON; the CLI's stdout carries one more byte, the trailing newline cmd_view0's println! adds to every lens, which the Python tool did not write - stated here, not hidden. The Python tool is deleted in this commit and tool-reference / instruments-declared / cli-surface-declared stay green; the snStpaDiagram Sensor and fbStpaDiagram Feedback are removed with it, because a Sensor declares a measure outside the CLI (D0363) and the diagram is now the cliControlStructure lens, whose channel the control structure derives from the CLI facts. This story resolves issue461 (the control-structure lens's feedback rows varied between runs with the tree unchanged - sensors now walked in item-name order, held by instrument_feedback_rows_are_in_one_order_whatever_the_map_order) and issue462 (the console's generic viewpoint panel fetched /api/computed/show for every renderer beginning keel show - vpCmd now strips the show token too) and issue463 (keel suite --touched measured its changed set to HEAD, so the verifier's pre-commit run of the gate's own set was EMPTY on this very sprint - touched.rs now measures from the merge-base to the working tree plus untracked files under keel-cli). On the live tree the render is byte-equal to the Python tool's once the CR bytes Python's text-mode stdout adds on Windows are removed (the verifier's first comparison read a 218-byte difference that was exactly one CR per line). The five D0285 properties are unit tests on the layout: no_two_segments_share_a_line, every_edge_is_labelled_with_what_passes, every_crossing_carries_a_hop, no_line_passes_through_a_box, control_leaves_bottom_left_and_feedback_enters_bottom_right; plus an_absent_role_is_named_in_the_legend_and_drawn_nowhere and a_non_structure_json_is_refused_not_drawn_empty. The console serves the SVG at /view/control-structure and the safety viewpoint's panel embeds it. The skill (both renderings), the process file, the registry, the instruments file, the CLI facts and CLAUDE.md name the binary command and no longer the tool. VERIFY as the verifier reports: keel suite --touched (the gate's own set, D0432) all passed; clippy -D warnings clean; keel validate, check-engine, guard --no-receipt green; sync-claude --check clean; the live byte comparison against the HEAD copy of the Python tool."; }
