    verification stpaDiagramInTheBinaryRefineGate : Test { :>> id = "880aa876-2970-4356-9641-8654958235ca"; :>> title = "Sprint 659 refine gate (DoR)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-10"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Five points: a thousand-line port whose correctness is judged byte for byte against the artefact it replaces, seven layout tests, four wiring sites (dispatch, render, serve route, console panel), a deletion with its doc-sync across eight files, and whatever the byte comparison turns up. Ready: dcStpaDiagramInTheBinary is head of whats-next after dcCommitDeltaView closed; its charter D0285 is accepted; the Python tool is a single file with no dependency beyond json/html/re, so the port is arithmetic and string building. Known before the tree was read: the positive case for the port is the fixture JSON whose Python SVG is the golden (equal bytes), the negative case is a JSON with no controllers array (refused, not drawn empty); the positive case for the determinism finding is sixty sensors in two independently seeded maps (with the sort removed the test fails on the first pair), the negative case is the sorted walk (five builds equal)."; }
