    verification stpaDiagramInTheBinaryImplementGate : Test { :>> id = "9e1a19d6-c5ca-4bc0-90c5-cb8a7c28390a"; :>> title = "Sprint 659 implement gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-10"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Built: keel-cli/src/view/stpa_diagram.rs - Num (Python int/float semantics: int op int stays int, any float or a division yields a float that prints as repr), Edge / Seg / BoxAt / Label / Layout, layout(&Value) -> Result<Layout, String> (the levels, the boxes, the control channels by 8px lanes, the feedback channels, the verticals at each box's bottom-left for control and bottom-right for feedback, the labels wrapped and placed with leaders, the crossings), svg(&Layout) with the hop arcs computed from Layout::crossings, render_json, control_structure_svg (ViewError::Track) and control_structure_html (the page with the light/dark palette the SVG's CSS variables resolve against). Wired: main.rs dispatch takes --svg on show control-structure; reports.rs render_html routes control-structure --mode graph to the page; serve.rs adds /view/control-structure; console.html's vpCmd strips keel show as well as keel (15 of 30 viewpoint renderers begin with keel show; before this change the generic panel fetched /api/computed/show and got 404 for every one of them - verified by serving a copy of the binary on 7791: GET /api/computed/show 404, GET /api/computed/control-structure 200, GET /view/control-structure 200 with one svg element) and embeds the diagram in an iframe when the command is control-structure. Deleted: .engine/tools/stpa_diagram.py; migrate.rs PORTABLE_TOOLS and init_smoke.rs no longer name it. Doc-sync: .engine/processes/stpa-diagram.sysml header, .engine/skills/stpa-diagram/SKILL.md and .claude/skills/stpa-diagram/SKILL.md, registry.sysml purpose, .tracking/architecture/engine-instruments.sysml (snStpaDiagram and fbStpaDiagram removed: the diagram is a CLI lens now, not an instrument outside it), CLAUDE.md section 2, cli_facts.rs and commands.sysml cliControlStructure invocation and synopsis. Root fix carried: control_structure.rs instrument_feedback walks the sensors in item-name order (it walked the HashMap) with instrument_feedback_rows_are_in_one_order_whatever_the_map_order as the test; after the fix three consecutive runs of the lens are identical (cmp) and the Rust render equals the Python render on the live JSON. Lints: the module allows the numeric-port lints at module level with the reason stated in its doc comment (the casts are the port, the names are the geometry's, every index is into a constant table or a map filled from the list the index came from); the rest were fixed. issue461 (lens nondeterministic, in-field) and issue462 (viewpoint panel unreachable for show-prefixed renderers, code-read then runtime-verified) recorded, both resolved by this sprint's story. Second root fix carried, from the verifier's first report: keel suite --touched read changed modules [] against a tree with twenty edited files, because compute diffed base...HEAD and HEAD equalled origin/main - the verifier had run the gate's set as nothing and reported outcome empty (issue463, in-field). touched.rs compute now diffs from the merge-base of the base and HEAD to the working tree and adds git ls-files --others under keel-cli; the same command then read eight stems including the untracked stpa_diagram module, and the_changed_set_is_the_working_trees_not_heads holds it (probed: fails against the old compute)."; }
