    verification stpaDiagramInTheBinaryRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "a0e06d6c-f1f5-443e-83ea-1856c3e089a4"; :>> title = "Sprint 659 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-10"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Autonomous retro (D0049). AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN: three Issues this sprint. issue463, the touched set measured to HEAD while the verifier runs before the commit: avoidable - the D0432 text says the set is computed from the changed paths and the implementation chose the committed ones; caught only because the verifier reported the receipt's counts (0 passed, 0 failed, outcome empty) instead of echoing the claim, which is precisely the D0425 division of labour doing its work; the control is the_changed_set_is_the_working_trees_not_heads - a scratch repo with a clean tree (known-negative, no stem) and then an uncommitted edit plus an untracked module (known-positive), probed against the old compute (fails on the positive) before the fix was stated. issue461, the lens's row order depending on HashMap seed: avoidable in principle - every lens that pushes rows from a map walk has this exposure - and not caught because nothing compared two runs of any lens byte for byte until a port needed to; the control is the test, and the class-wide question (which other lenses walk a map into rows) is a candidate backlog item rather than a fix smuggled in here. issue462, the generic viewpoint panel stripping only keel from a renderer string: avoidable by a test that fetched every declared viewpoint's renderer through the panel's own path; no such test exists, so the fix is a two-token regex and the residual is that the console's JS has no runtime test in the suite. Finding 3, about D0425: the verifier-recorder split held for the second sprint running and the primary's time went to the port; the one place the split leaked was the clippy census, which the primary ran itself because it needed the messages to fix the code - that is substance, not checking. Finding 5, found at the commit: the verifier's keel guard --no-receipt ran over the unstaged tree and reported ALL PASS, and the pre-commit hook refused the same edits on process-change - the index-reading guards scan git diff --cached, so before git add they scan nothing (issue464, in-field, High; resolver dcGuardReadsTheWorkingTreeOutsideTheHook: outside a hook the locked-surface guards read the working tree). The stpa-diagram process file's renderer doc-sync needed a marked Decision, recorded as D0433 and co-committed. Finding 4, hygiene: the one heredoc denial (a backslash-n in a Python patch) was followed immediately by the Write tool; every other patch went through textpatch with an anchor and none missed."; }
